<title>USA: U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS - Issues to Watch - Jan 24.</title>
<headline>U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS - Issues to Watch - Jan 24.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stocks to watch this morning:</p>
<p>-- PepsiCo said it will spin off its Pizza Hut, Taco Bell and Kentucky Fried Chicken restaurant businesses to shareholders. The announcement came after the stock market closed Thursday.</p>
<p>Pepsico shares rose 2-3/8 to 34-1/4 in heavy trading.</p>
<p>-- General Motors Corp could raise its dividend and begin a huge stock buyback program Monday, the Wall Street Journal reported. GM shares closed at 62.  </p>
<p>-- Gateway 2000 said it expects 1997 margins to remain relatively flat compared to 1996 levels. The company posted a 50 percent rise in fourth quarter earnings. Shares closed at 63-5/8.</p>
<p>-- Schult Homes Corp said winter weather should hurt demand for mobile homes in the quarter ending in March, more so than in the milder winters of the past two years.</p>
<p>Shares closed at 23.</p>
</text>
